Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:22:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] library: the MCP check starts a bare command a version
 manager has (#2685)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What changed
- The Library's health check started a stdio server with the command as
  typed, and exec finds a bare name on the PATH the process carries. A
  magpie started from a shortcut doesn't have a version manager's Node
  on it, so a server a terminal runs through fnm — npx -y pkg — failed
  the check as "notfound" while the agents ran it fine: they look their
  own CLIs up through proc.FindTool, PATH first, then the folders a
  user's tools are installed in (#839, #1482). The check now looks a
  bare command up the same way before starting it; a command with a
  path in it, absolute or relative, still starts as typed, resolved
  where the command runs.
- fnm's folders were missing from that lookup on Windows: UserBinDirs
  had npm, bun, Volta, pnpm and mise, and fnm's folders were computed
  in a //go:build !windows file. The version enumeration and fnm's
  layout move into a shared nodever.go that takes where a version's
  programs sit — installation/bin, or on Windows the installation
  itself, npx.cmd with no bin folder — and UserBinDirs now walks
  FNM_DIR's folder, else %APPDATA%\fnm, the default alias ahead of the
  versions by number.

Run
- TestCheckStdioVersionManagerNode (internal/library): a fake MCP
  server copied to ~/.local/share/fnm/node-versions/v22.12.0/
  installation/bin/npx, PATH without it. Red on 717b69f7 — notfound,
  the report's 找不到 npx — green after; -race -count=3 green.
  Ablation: mcp_check.go restored to 717b69f7 with the test kept, red
  again; fix back, green.
- TestFnmBinsShapes (internal/proc) takes fnmBins through both shapes'
  layout on this machine, default alias hoisted; the nvm and fnm
  ordering tests stay green after the move. TestUserBinDirsFnm
  (//go:build windows: %APPDATA%\fnm's versions highest first, FNM_DIR's
  ahead of them, FindTool("npx") = v22's npx.cmd) compiles here
  (GOOS=windows go vet and go test -c) and was not run on Windows.
- gofmt -l clean; go vet ./..., GOOS=linux go vet -tags nogui ./... and
  GOOS=windows go vet ./... clean; go build, GOOS=linux go build -tags
  nogui and GOOS=windows go build; go test -tags nogui ./... green
  except internal/gui's TestProxyCheckSaysAProxyPassedBy, red on
  unmodified main too (a fake proxy answers 502 saying it was never
  asked; not this change's).
- Not verified: a real Windows desktop.

